        "original_id": "c4b00479-cacf-58c4-b180-7fd5b967c06a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Liddell, Harold Abrahams\n- Works: Chariots of Fire\n- Events: 1924 Olympics\n- Roles: athlete, rugby union international player, missionary\n- Concepts: religious beliefs, prejudice, Christianity, Judaism\n\nFacts:\n- Eric Henry Liddell was born on 16 January 1902 and died on 21 February 1945.\n- Chariots of Fire tells a fact-based story about two athletes in the 1924 Olympics: Eric Liddell and Harold Abrahams.\n- Eric Liddell was a Scottish athlete, a rugby union international player, and a missionary.\n- In Chariots of Fire, Eric Liddell is described as a devout Scottish Christian who runs for the glory of God.\n- In Chariots of Fire, Harold Abrahams is described as an English Jew who runs to overcome prejudice.\n- Eric Liddell chose his religious beliefs over competing in an Olympic race held on a Sunday.",
